<https://w3id.org/security#capabilityInvocationMethod> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://www.w3.org/TR/did-core/#capability-invocation> .
<https://w3id.org/security#capabilityInvocationMethod> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The capabilityInvocation property is used to express a verification relationship which an entity can use to invoke capabilities as the DID subject or on behalf of the DID subject." .
<https://w3id.org/security#capabilityInvocationMethod> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://www.w3.org/ns/did#VerificationMethod> .
<https://w3id.org/security#capabilityInvocationMethod> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Property> .
<https://w3id.org/security#capabilityDelegationMethod> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://www.w3.org/TR/did-core/#capability-delegation> .
<https://w3id.org/security#capabilityDelegationMethod> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The capabilityDelegation property is used to express a verification relationship which an entity can use to grant capabilities as the DID subject or on behalf of the DID subject to other capability invokers. " .
<https://w3id.org/security#capabilityDelegationMethod> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://www.w3.org/ns/did#VerificationMethod> .
<https://w3id.org/security#capabilityDelegationMethod> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Property> .
<https://w3id.org/security#keyAgreementMethod> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://www.w3.org/TR/did-core/#key-agreement> .
<https://w3id.org/security#keyAgreementMethod> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The keyAgreement property is used to express a verification relationship which an entity can use to engage in key agreement protocols on behalf of the DID subject." .
<https://w3id.org/security#keyAgreementMethod> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://www.w3.org/ns/did#VerificationMethod> .
<https://w3id.org/security#keyAgreementMethod> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Property> .
<https://w3id.org/security#assertionMethod> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://www.w3.org/TR/did-core/#assertion> .
<https://w3id.org/security#assertionMethod> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The assertionMethod property is used to express a verification relationship which indicates that a verification method can be used to verify a proof that a statement was asserted on behalf of the DID subject." .
<https://w3id.org/security#assertionMethod> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://www.w3.org/ns/did#VerificationMethod> .
<https://w3id.org/security#assertionMethod> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Property> .
<https://w3id.org/security#authenticationMethod> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://www.w3.org/TR/did-core/#authentication> .
<https://w3id.org/security#authenticationMethod> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Authentication is a verification relationship which an entity can use to prove it is the DID subject or acting on behalf of the DID Subject as a DID Controller." .
<https://w3id.org/security#authenticationMethod> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://www.w3.org/ns/did#VerificationMethod> .
<https://w3id.org/security#authenticationMethod> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Property> .
<https://w3id.org/security#verificationMethod> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://www.w3.org/TR/did-core/#verification-methods> .
<https://w3id.org/security#verificationMethod> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A generic method to refer to a Verification Method" .
<https://w3id.org/security#verificationMethod> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://www.w3.org/ns/did#VerificationMethod> .
<https://w3id.org/security#verificationMethod> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Property> .
<https://w3id.org/security#controller> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "An entity that is authorized to make changes to a DID Document" .
<https://w3id.org/security#controller> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://www.w3.org/TR/did-core/#control> .
